# Terrain and placement share one grid, so the board is what it looks like.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: hz-07-standing-room
number: 207
name: Standing Room
description: Six enemies, every one of them standing beside the thing that kills it, and exactly one round before they all walk away from it.
design: Hazard Pressure 7 of 10 — six enemies, one round, four activations.
design: Nothing starts ON a hazard — the format forbids it — but everything starts NEXT to one, and on its own activation it walks away from it. Player A pushes away from itself; Player B only pulls toward itself, so A and B are shopping from two different shelves: A wants the hazard on the far side of an enemy, B wants it in between.
design: No high ground here on purpose: the question is what you can convert before they move.

spawn l = Lobber
spawn h = Husk
spawn s = Stalker

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  .....l.h.
  .....O.^B
  ....s...B
  ^h......B
  .........
  A.....h#.
  AAh^.....
